---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { articleNode } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Life Lessons from Kasra Dash';
const description =
  'Five life lessons from Kasra Dash in his own words: bar work, moving cities young, stepping out of the comfort zone, finding a mentor and choosing the five people around you.';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Life Lessons', href: '/life-lessons/' },
];

/* Kasra's own lessons (voice notes, 12 Aug 2026), rewritten as fluent written
 * prose at his request: same five lessons in his learning order, first person,
 * personality and every concrete detail kept, spoken scaffolding cut. */

const canonical = `${SITE_URL}/life-lessons/`;
const graphNodes = [
  articleNode({ canonical, headline: 'Life Lessons from Kasra Dash', description }),
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} path="/life-lessons/" breadcrumbs={crumbs} {graphNodes} type="article">
  <main>
    <section class="border-b border-tint-border bg-tint">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
        <Breadcrumbs {crumbs} />
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Life Lessons from Kasra Dash</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Five lessons, in the order I learnt them. For other entrepreneurs, and maybe one day for kids who want to build something of their own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <div class="reading-well prose prose-well max-w-3xl p-5 sm:p-8 lg:p-12">
        <h2>1. Work somewhere public facing</h2>
        <p>
          Everyone should do a stint somewhere public facing, like a bar. You meet interesting characters and, for lack of a better word, assholes. Both build character. Life does not run in straight lines, and the difficult people keep turning up: in person, as keyboard warriors, as YouTube trolls.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Move to another city young</h2>
        <p>
          After university I moved from Scotland to Northampton for a job, knowing literally no one. Leaving the city that holds your mates and your family forces you to become more outgoing.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Step out of your comfort zone</h2>
        <p>
          My first web design client, at eighteen or nineteen, wanted an e-commerce store. I had only ever built brochure sites. I convinced him anyway: six months of work, no AI to lean on in 2018, and about £5,000 at the end. Good money back then, especially for me.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Find a mentor</h2>
        <p>
          At nineteen or twenty I found James Dooley. He had already done what I was trying to do, knew the outcomes, and fast-tracked my path. If university is not for you, find a mentor. A good one is worth its weight in gold.
        </p>

        <h2>5. You are the average of the five people you spend the most time with</h2>
        <p>
          People say they want more, then keep company that pulls them down rather than drags them up. I was lucky: I picked five successful people, and they pushed me up a level. Friends doing six million a year when you do two know the downfalls, and you can always ask. It works beyond money too: surround yourself with fitness people and they push you in the gym.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-tint-border bg-tint py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 text-center sm:px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">More of the story</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-muted">
          The longer version lives on the about page, and the conferences these years led to are on the speaking page.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a href="/about-kasra-dash/" class="btn-gradient px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold shadow-lg shadow-brand-500/25 transition hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-brand-500/40">
            About Kasra Dash
          </a>
          <a href="/speaking/" class="rounded-full border border-tint-border px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ink transition hover:border-brand-500 hover:bg-brand-500/10">
            Speaking
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
